;; refuse: unsupported op :def
;; P1.4: `def` inside a function body (the :def op). Neither target program does it.
;; The backend must refuse this with a clear "unsupported op :def" error.
;; refuse-llvm: none
;; The llvm lane lowers a def inside a fn, so there it behaves as native.
(defn make [] (def late 42) late)
(println (make))
